<section class="page-intro shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">Help &amp; support</p><h1>Start with the simple answer.</h1>
  <div class="page-lede"><p>Installation guidance, permission explanations, and honest release status for StylePort.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="support-layout shell">
  <aside class="support-card"><p class="eyebrow">Need a hand?</p><h2>Report a problem</h2><p>Include your macOS version, Safari version, StylePort version, and the smallest style that reproduces the issue. Never include private browsing data.</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:{{ site.supportEmail }}" data-tinylytics-event="contact.email" data-tinylytics-event-value="support">Email {{ site.supportEmail }}</a></aside>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details><summary>Why is StylePort both an app and a Safari extension?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Safari Web Extensions are packaged inside a macOS app. The app installs the extension and gives you a visible place to confirm its status; the extension supplies the browser toolbar and UserCSS features.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does Safari say StylePort can read and alter webpages?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Applying CSS requires access to the webpages you choose. StylePort uses that permission to match a page and insert your selected CSS. It does not use the permission to create or transmit a browsing history.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where are my styles stored?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Styles, variables, and preferences live in Safari’s local extension storage on your Mac. StylePort has no account or developer-operated cloud database.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I import an existing Stylus backup?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>StylePort is built on the mature Stylus engine and the migration path for compatible backups is part of the release work. Always keep your original backup until a restore has been verified.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I beta test StylePort now?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Yes. The signed direct edition is available, and the public TestFlight beta remains open for testing the Apple-distributed edition on a Mac running macOS 14 or later. <a href="{{ site.testFlightUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="app.testflight" data-tinylytics-event-value="testflight-beta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join the StylePort TestFlight beta</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How will updates work?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>{% if directRelease.available %}The direct-download edition uses Sparkle with a signed update feed and Ed25519 verification.{% else %}The public TestFlight beta is currently the only available edition. The future direct-download edition uses Sparkle with a signed update feed and Ed25519 verification.{% endif %} You can check manually or choose automatic checks while the StylePort companion app is open; automatic installation stays off. The App Store edition uses Apple’s update system and does not include Sparkle.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will StylePort be available for iPhone or iPad?<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>The first release targets macOS Safari. An iOS and iPadOS container is on the roadmap after the Mac experience and release process are reliable.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section shell install-guide">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Direct edition</p><h2>Install in four steps.</h2></div>
  <ol><li><span>1</span><strong>Download</strong><p>Get the <a href="{{ directRelease.archivePath | url }}" download data-tinylytics-event="app.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="relaybyte-direct">signed and notarized StylePort ZIP</a> from this site.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Move</strong><p>Open the ZIP, move StylePort to your Applications folder, and open it.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Enable</strong><p>Turn on StylePort in Safari Settings → Extensions.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Style</strong><p>Grant the sites you choose, then import your CSS or UserCSS.</p></li></ol>
</section>
